{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Give ear.</b> I have already explained in my book that the word האזינו is from the root of אזן (ear), as though he said: incline an ear." "And I have already informed you that the Gaon [Saadia] said that the sense of <b>the heavens</b> is the angels, and the sense of <b>the earth</b> is the people of the earth. Or: the testimony of the rain that comes down from the heavens and the earth gives its yield. And the correct view in my eyes is that the essence is because they stand forever, as it says, \"Hear, O mountains\" (Micah 6:1), likewise the stone of Joshua, and there it is written that it heard. And I have already hinted to you concerning the soul of man, that it is an intermediary between the higher and the lower, and it images everything upon the form of its palace. And even to understand also Her who sits in the palace. Therefore it exalts the lower and lowers the higher."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The phrase 'also Her who sits in the palace' is elliptic and textually difficult; translated hyper-literally. 'Book' in comment 0 may refer to an earlier work or to his grammar treatise; resolved generically without expansion."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:25:47.584731669Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}